 17592186240813 13194139533392 17592186045585 true] [17592186119886 1038 #edb/ref 17592186240814 13194139533392 17592186045585 true] [17592186119887 1038 #edb/ref 17592186240816 13194139533392 17592186045585 true] [17592186119887 1038 #edb/ref 17592186240820 13194139533392 17592186045585 true] [17592186119887 1038 #edb/ref 17592186240821 13194139533392 17592186045585 true] [17592186119887 1038 #edb/ref 17592186240822 13194139533392 17592186045585 true] [17592186119887 1038 #edb/ref 17592186240824 13194139533392 17592186045585 true] [17592186119887 1038 #edb/ref 17592186240825 13194139533392 17592186045585 true] [17592186119888 1038 #edb/ref 17592186240842 13194139533392 17592186045585 true] [17592186119888 1038 #edb/ref 17592186240843 13194139533392 17592186045585 true] [17592186119888 1038 #edb/ref 17592186240844 13194139533392 17592186045585 true] [17592186119888 1038 #edb/ref 17592186240845 13194139533392 17592186045585 true] [17592186119888 1038 #edb/ref 17592186240849 13194139533392 17592186045585 true] [17592186119889 1038 #edb/ref 17592186240863 13194139533392 17592186045585 true] [17592186119889 1038 #edb/ref 17592186240864 13194139533392 17592186045585 true] [17592186119889 1038 #edb/ref 17592186240865 13194139533392 17592186045585 true] [17592186119889 1038 #edb/ref 17592186240866 13194139533392 17592186045585 true] [17592186119889 1038 #edb/ref 17592186240867 13194139533392 17592186045585 true] [17592186119890 1038 #edb/ref 17592186241082 13194139533392 17592186045585 true] [17592186119891 1038 #edb/ref 17592186241141 13194139533392 17592186045585 true] [17592186119892 1038 #edb/ref 17592186241129 13194139533392 17592186045585 true] [17592186119892 1038 #edb/ref 17592186241130 13194139533392 17592186045585 true] [17592186119929 1038 #edb/ref 17592186241032 13194139533392 17592186045585 true] [17592186119929 1038 #edb/ref 17592186241033 13194139533392 17592186045585 true] [17592186119929 1038 #edb/ref 17592186241034 13194139533392 17592186045585 true] [17592186119931 1038 #edb/ref 17592186241037 13194139533392 17592186045585 true] [17592186119931 1038 #edb/ref 17592186241039 13194139533392 17592186045585 true] [17592186119931 1038 #edb/ref 17592186241042 13194139533392 17592186045585 true] [17592186119931 1038 #edb/ref 17592186241044 13194139533392 17592186045585 true] [17592186120079 1068 #edb/ref 17592186116651 13194139533392 17592186045585 false] [17592186120079 1068 #edb/ref 17592186240760 13194139533392 17592186045585 true] [17592186120079 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533392 17592186045585 true] [17592186120079 1071 "$$\n{∬}_{D}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}A,\\,D={(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 1,\\,0\\le v\\le \\pi }\n$$\n\nThe integral above gives the surface area of the parametric surface $r(u,v)=⟨2u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,3u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,u⟩$ for $0\\le u\\le 1$ and $0\\le v\\le \\pi .$ What is the missing expression?" 13194139533392 17592186045585 true] [17592186120079 1071 "$∬_(D)AAAAAAAAdA, D = {(u, v): 0 \\le u \\le 1, 0 \\le v \\le π}$\n\nThe integral above gives the surface area of the parametric surface $r(u, v) = ⟨2u\\sin v, 3u\\cos v, u⟩$ for $0 \\le u \\le 1$ and $0 \\le v \\le π$. What is the missing expression?" 13194139533392 17592186045585 false] [17592186120079 1074 "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface area of $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(3u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,3\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,1⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(3u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,-3u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡v & 3\\operatorname{cos}⁡v & 1 \\\\ 2u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v & -3u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{cos}⁡v & 1 \\\\ -3u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡v & 1 \\\\ 2u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡v & 3\\operatorname{cos}⁡v \\\\ 2u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v & -3u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,2u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,-6u{sin}^{2}⁡v-6u{cos}^{2}⁡v⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,2u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,-6u⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖ & =‖⟨3u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,2u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,-6u⟩‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(3u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v)^{2}+(2u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v)^{2}+(-6u)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9{u}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡v+4{u}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡v+36{u}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(5{u}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡v+4{u}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡v)+4{u}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡v+36{u}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5{u}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡v+4{u}^{2}({sin}^{2}⁡v+{cos}^{2}⁡v)+36{u}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5{u}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡v+4{u}^{2}+36{u}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5{u}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡v+40{u}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5{u}^{2}({sin}^{2}⁡v+8)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5{u}^{2}}\\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡v+8} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5}u\\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡v+8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $\\sqrt{{u}^{2}}=u$ since $u\\ge 0$ on $D.$\n\nTherefore, the surface area is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{5}u\\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡v+8}\\,\\text{d}A\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533392 17592186045585 true] [17592186120082 1068 #edb/ref 17592186116669 13194139533392 17592186045585 false] [17592186120082 1068 #edb/ref 17592186240522 13194139533392 17592186045585 true] [17592186120082 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533392 17592186045585 true] [17592186120082 1071 "$$\nD=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ -3 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 12 & 8 & 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n \n\nIf $D=LU$ is the LU decomposition of the matrix $D$ given above, what is the value of ${l}_{32}\\cdot {u}_{22}?$" 13194139533392 17592186045585 true] [17592186120082 1071 "$D = \\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ -3 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 12 & 8 & 5\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nIf $D = LU$ is the LU decomposition of the matrix $D$ given above, what is the value of $l_{32} \\cdot u_{22}$?" 13194139533392 17592186045585 false] [17592186120082 1074 "Let's apply our standard LU factorization algorithm.\n\nWe reduce the matrix $D$ to row echelon form to obtain the matrix $U,$ as usual. However, instead of writing zeros below the main diagonal, we will instead write down the entries of the matrix $L.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ -3 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 12 & 8 & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+1{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -4 & -1 \\\\ 12 & 8 & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -4 & -1 \\\\ \\,\\,4\\,\\, & 16 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+4{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -4 & -1 \\\\ \\,\\,4\\,\\, & -4 & -3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\nL=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -4 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,U=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -4 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${l}_{32}=-4$ and ${u}_{22}=-4,$ we get\n\n$$\n{l}_{32}\\cdot {u}_{22}=(-4)\\cdot (-4)=16.\n$$" 13194139533392 17592186045585 true] [17592186120084 1068 #edb/ref 17592186116681 13194139533392 17592186045585 false] [17592186120084 1068 #edb/ref 17592186240778 13194139533392 17592186045585 true] [17592186120084 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533392 17592186045585 true] [17592186120084 1071 "Find the surface area of the parametric surface defined by the equations\n\n$x = 2u - v, y = 3u + 2, z = u + 2v$\n\nfor $0 \\le u \\le 1$ and $-1 \\le v \\le 1$." 13194139533392 17592186045585 false] [17592186120084 1071 "Find the surface area of the parametric surface defined by the equations \n\n$$\nx=2u-v,\\,y=3u+2,\\,z=u+2v\n$$\n\nfor $0\\le u\\le 1$ and $-1\\le v\\le 1.$" 13194139533392 17592186045585 true] [17592186120084 1074 "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface area of $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn vector form, our surface has the equation \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨2u-v,\\,3u+2,\\,u+2v⟩.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2u-v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(3u+2),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u+2v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,\\,3,\\,1⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2u-v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(3u+2),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u+2v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,\\,0,\\,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨6,\\,-5,\\,3⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖ & =‖⟨6,\\,-5,\\,3⟩‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{6}^{2}+(-5)^{2}+{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{36+25+9} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{70}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, let's denote\n\n$$\nD={(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 1,\\,-1\\le v\\le 1}.\n$$\n\nThen, the surface area is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{70}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\sqrt{70}{∬}_{D}\\text{ }\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\sqrt{70}\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{70}\\cdot 1\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{70}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533392 17592186045585 true] [17592186120085 1068 #edb/ref 17592186116687 13194139533392 17592186045585 false] [17592186120085 1068 #edb/ref 17592186240640 13194139533392 17592186045585 true] [17592186120085 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533392 17592186045585 true] [17592186120085 1071 "Find the surface area of the part of the parametric surface $r(u, v) = ⟨ - u + v, u - 2v, 3v⟩$ that is subject to the constraint $u^{2} + v^{2} \\le 4$." 13194139533392 17592186045585 false] [17592186120085 1071 "Find the surface area of the part of the parametric surface $r(u,v)=⟨-u+v,\\,u-2v,\\,3v⟩$ that is subject to the constraint ${u}^{2}+{v}^{2}\\le 4.$" 13194139533392 17592186045585 true] [17592186120085 1074 "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface area of $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(-u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u-2v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(3v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,\\,1,\\,0⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(-u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u-2v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(3v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,-2,\\,3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,3,\\,1⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖ & =‖⟨3,\\,3,\\,1⟩‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{3}^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+9+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{19}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, notice that the region ${u}^{2}+{v}^{2}\\le 4$ corresponds to the disk\n\n$$\nD={(u,v)\\,:\\,{u}^{2}+{v}^{2}\\le 4},\n$$\n\nof radius $2.$\n\nTherefore, the surface area is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{19}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\sqrt{19}{∬}_{D}\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\sqrt{19}\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{19}\\cdot (\\pi \\cdot {2}^{2}) \\\\  & =4\\pi \\sqrt{19}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533392 17592186045585 true] [17592186120086 1068 #edb/ref 17592186116692 13194139533392 17592186045585 false] [17592186120086 1068 #edb/ref 17592186240681 13194139533392 17592186045585 true] [17592186120086 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533392 17592186045585 true] [17592186120086 1071 "Consider the LU decomposition of the matrix $A$ and the vector $b$, given by\n$A = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}_(⏟)_(L)\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}_(⏟)_(U), b = \\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}$.\nIf $⟨x_{1}, x_{2}⟩$ and $⟨y_{1}, y_{2}⟩$ are the solutions to the systems $Ax = b$ and $Ly = b$ respectively, what is the value of $x_{1} \\cdot y_{1}$?" 13194139533392 17592186045585 false] [17592186120086 1071 "Consider the LU decomposition of the matrix $A$ and the vector $b,$ given by\n\n$$\nA={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{L}{{[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{U},\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $⟨{x}_{1},{x}_{2}⟩$ and $⟨{y}_{1},{y}_{2}⟩$ are the solutions to the systems $Ax=b$ and $Ly=b$ respectively, what is the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {y}_{1}?$" 13194139533392 17592186045585 true] [17592186120086 1074 "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $Ux=y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nL{{(Ux)}_{⏟}}_{y}=b\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the two systems in turn.\n\n- First, we solve $Ly=b.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=b=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=-1 \\\\ -{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is ${y}_{1}=-1$ and ${y}_{2}=2.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\ny=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n- Next, we solve $Ux=y.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=y=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-3{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}=-1 \\\\ {x}_{2}=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is ${x}_{2}=2$ and ${x}_{1}=-1.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}\\cdot {y}_{1}=(-1)\\cdot (-1)=1.$" 13194139533392 17592186045585 true] [17592186124640 1038 #edb/ref 17592186241040 13194139533392 17592186045585 true] [17592186124648 1038 #edb/ref 17592186241046 13194139533392 17592186045585 true] [17592186124648 1038 #edb/ref 17592186241048 13194139533392 17592186045585 true] [17592186124648 1038 #edb/ref 17592186241049 13194139533392 17592186045585 true] [17592186124660 1038 #edb/ref 17592186240975 13194139533392 17592186045585 true] [17592186124660 1038 #edb/ref 17592186240976 13194139533392 17592186045585 true] [17592186124661 1038 #edb/ref 17592186241047 13194139533392 17592186045585 true] [17592186129090 1038 #edb/ref 17592186240874 13194139533392 17592186045585 true] [17592186129090 1038 #edb/ref 17592186240879 13194139533392 17592186045585 true] [17592186129090 1038 #edb/ref 17592186240881 13194139533392 17592186045585 true] [17592186129091 1038 #edb/ref 17592186240870 13194139533392 17