nce in the counterclockwise direction, starting from $(h+a,k).$\n\nIn our case, the ellipse is centered at the point $(-2,-3),$ $a=5$ and $b=3.$ Therefore, the parametric equations of the ellipse are \n\n$$\nx=5\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -2,\\,y=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -3,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$" 13194139533392 17592186045585 true] [17592186241171 1068 #edb/ref 17592186240703 13194139533392 17592186045585 true] [17592186241171 1069 "q-106399" 13194139533392 17592186045585 true] [17592186241171 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533392 17592186045585 true] [17592186241171 1071 "![](images/49/494e360a4c22d96feb811de6ee507996a11be65ee346d837debcb927c0d28434.png)\n\nConsider the ellipse centered at $(-3,2)$ with horizontal radius $7$ and vertical radius $4,$ as shown above. Which of the following sets of parametric equations, defined for $\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ),$  traverse the ellipse once in the counterclockwise direction starting at the point $A(4,2)?$" 13194139533392 17592186045585 true] [17592186241171 1072 #uuid "face32c2-838a-5a8c-a2dc-dfdf5610f42d" 13194139533392 17592186045585 true] [17592186241171 1074 "The parametric equations of an ellipse centered at the point $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ are\n\n$$\nx=a\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +h,\\,y=b\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +k,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$\n\nUnder this parametrization, the ellipse is traversed once in the counterclockwise direction, starting from $(h+a,k).$\n\nIn our case, the ellipse is centered at the point $(-3,2),$ $a=7$ and $b=4.$ Therefore, the parametric equations of the ellipse are \n\n$$\nx=7\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -3,\\,y=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +2,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$" 13194139533392 17592186045585 true] [17592186241172 1068 #edb/ref 17592186240665 13194139533392 17592186045585 true] [17592186241172 1069 "q-106400" 13194139533392 17592186045585 true] [17592186241172 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 1