omain of the parameter $\\theta ?$" 13194139533392 17592186045585 true] [17592186241173 1072 #uuid "d3351acb-0711-5b2c-8212-2f838f3d3d1d" 13194139533392 17592186045585 true] [17592186241173 1074 "The parametric equations of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ are\n\n$$\nx=a\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=b\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$\n\nIn our case, $a=5$ and $b=2.$ Therefore, the parametric equations of the *full* ellipse are\n\n$$\nx=5\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$\n\nTo restrict the parameterization to a quarter-ellipse, we associate the parameter $\\theta $ with the central angle formed by a point $(x,y)$ on the elipse and the $x$-axis. \n\n![](images/74/74714486ad225aba7111329be0c3853b7b922a852df450b057632e73fce5be6d.png)\n\nWe can see that if we restrict $\\theta $ to $[0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}]$, we get the quarter-ellipse.\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the quarter-ellipse are \n\n$$\nx=5\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\theta \\in [0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}].\n$$" 13194139533392 17592186045585 true] [17592186241174 1068 #edb/ref 17592186240392 13194139533392 17592186045585 true] [17592186241174 1069 "q-106403" 13194139533392 17592186045585 true] [17592186241174 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533392 17592186045585 true] [17592186241174 1071 "![](images/5b/5b344621d5500d3253295c970b0a7557b80f4d2cbfa66c17ba6f8868c1424c08.png)\n\nThe quarter-ellipse above is defined by the parametric equations \n\n$$\nx=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nWhat is the domain of the parameter $\\theta ?$" 13194139533392 17592186045585 true] [17592186241174 1072 #uuid "c9cfc762-69e6-5d11-8bd6-6402006ff4d5" 13194139533392 17592186045585 true] [17592186241174 1074 "The parametric equations of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizo